Z||000001||fiero56||02-25-2000||10:50 AM||||I've had my car almost 1 year, just a few more days. I don't know how many winters it has seen in the past, but I have been very surprised at the small amounts of rust it does have. Through the middle of winter, I never got a chance to wash the poor salt covered car, but when I did, I found new scratches in the paint, and a spot below the gas fill where I spilled a little gas and it ate the paint.<BR>Now it needs a thorough polishing and waxing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula||02-25-2000||12:52 PM||||To determine how many winters your car has been through subtract the year of the car from 1999.  Example..... 1999 - 1988 = 11, the car has been through 11 winters.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||02-25-2000||05:30 PM||||Very good, Formula!  That was gonna be my response until I saw that you beat me to it.  Good one!||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||02-25-2000||08:08 PM||||Yeah, yeah, I know, I should have seen that one coming. What I meant to say, was how many winters on the road. My Fiero has lived in the same city in Ohio it's entire life. I bought it from a guy on the north side of the city, and I live in the south side.<BR>Since it is an '88 that was purchased in the summer, would that mean it has seen 12 winters? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
